   "question": "The text claims Er and Ce are incorporated in the co-doped particles, with Er present as Er3+ and Ce present as a surface Ce3+/Ce4+ mixture. Do the XPS panels F6c and F6d support this claim?",
   "answer_key": "No. The Ce 3d region (F6d) is noise with no resolved peaks at the marked u/v positions, so no Ce3+/Ce4+ mixture can be read off it, and the Er 4d fitted envelope (F6c) sits well above the noisy data, so the fit is not grounded in the actual signal either (o21).",
